<title>UK: Labour gives Babcock Rosyth refit work.</title>
<headline>Labour gives Babcock Rosyth refit work.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>In his first decision as Labour's Defence Secretary, George Robertson endorsed the second major refit of HMS Sceptre, one of five Swiftsure Class nuclear powered, hunter killer submarines.</p>
<p>The refit will be undertaken at Rosyth Royal Dockyard in Scotland at a cost of more than 120 million pounds.</p>
<p>Rosyth is owned by Babcock International Group Plc which bought it in November.</p>
<p>The contract will sustain employment and work at the dockyard over coming years, Robertson said in a statement.</p>
</text>
